{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And YHWH came down.</b> Now I state a general principle on which your heart may rely until I arrive, with HaShem's help, at the section Ki Tissa, for there I shall explain deep matters to you most well. Know that the soul of man is supernal and honored, and it is from the middle world, while the body is from the lower world. And there is no speaking being in the lower world except man alone. Also, man the listener understands that the one speaking to him wishes to convey to him what is in his heart. And the intelligent one cannot invent a language other than the one known and extant, and all languages are built upon the pattern of the form of man, which is composite: of the soul, which is not a body, and of the body, which is composed of four elements. Now when one man speaks to another in human speech in a language he knows, he understands his words and their pattern in their structure. And if one wishes to speak of things lower than human beings, he must elevate their rank and assign them the form of human beings until the listener understands. Therefore it says: the top of the earth (Proverbs 8:26); the top of the dust of the world (ibid.); the earth opened her mouth (Numbers 16:32); also thigh — the thigh of the earth (Jeremiah 6:22); the hand of the Jordan (Numbers 13:29); in the heart of the sea (above 15:8); and many like these. And all this is in the language of parable, for the sea has no heart. Furthermore, they assign a limb of the body as the likeness of the whole body, as it says: Death and life are in the hand of the tongue (Proverbs 18:21), and many like these. And when a person wishes to speak of beings more exalted than he, from the upper world, he lowers their rank until they resemble man, as though they are in the form of man, so that the listener may understand. It says: and the man Gabriel (Daniel 9:21); my knees and my joints; and the sound of his words like the sound of a multitude (ibid. 10:6). And this path they hold even for the Most High of the Most Highs. It says: and a helmet of salvation on His head (Isaiah 59:17); for the mouth of YHWH has spoken (ibid. 1:20); the eyes of YHWH are toward the righteous, and His ears toward their cry; the face of YHWH against evildoers (Psalms 34:16–17); and under His feet (below 24:10); and in this manner — and YHWH came down; and Elohim went up (Genesis 17:22); for all is full of His glory. And in the section Ki Tissa I shall give you a parable by which you can understand the reason for descent and ascent." "<b>And the meaning of ויקרא.</b> That HaShem called him so that Israel might see the greatness of Moses' rank, that he reached the top of the mountain where the Glory was, and that his words were heard from within the fire that was there."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The phrase וזרעותיו ומרגלתיו in the middle of the comment appears to be a textual corruption or fragment; it is unclear whether it belongs with the preceding Daniel 9:21 citation or intruded from a marginal note. Translated hyper-literally as rendered in the Hebrew."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:08.155926440Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}